        "Andreas Wallraff",
        "Robert J. Schoelkopf"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Circuit quantum electrodynamics established a powerful and experimentally controllable platform for studying light–matter interaction and became a foundation of superconducting quantum information processing.",
        "attribution": "Blais developed the theoretical framework, while Wallraff and Schoelkopf led pivotal experimental demonstrations and development of the platform.",
        "maturity": "The core physics is well verified and the platform has developed rapidly into a major research and technology area.",
